{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Symptom\n\nThe hourly LaunchAgent `com.navapbc.rebar-dev-update`, which keeps this host's **global**\n`rebar` / `rebar-mcp` aligned to `origin/main`, has failed 120+ consecutive times and is\nstill failing. The global build is pinned at `cdfd7d94dc2fe7671a7eba48e31f36c30f39235c`\n(2026-08-28) — 201 commits behind `origin/main` at the latest check, and climbing hourly.\n`launchctl list` reports last exit status 1 for the agent.\n\nEvery hourly run logs the same rejection:\n\n```\nerror: Required uv version `==0.12.7` does not match the running version `0.12.9`\ncandidate ebbcd7a030d6... rejected at sync; current left untouched\ncandidate-rejection streak now 122 (latest stage: sync)\n```\n\n## Root cause\n\n`~/.local/bin/rebar-dev-update.sh:18` hardcodes `UV_BIN` to an absolute Homebrew path and\n`:120` orders PATH to keep it authoritative. That premise has INVERTED: Homebrew's uv is now\n0.12.9, past the repository's exact `required-version = \"==0.12.7\"`, while the\n`~/.local/bin` standalone sits at 0.12.7. The guard written to stop a stale uv being\nselected is now the mechanism selecting one. Substituting the other absolute path\nre-inverts the moment that side updates first. Full forensics — the `febd` precedent, the\nSNS failure, and the impact measurement — are preserved in the ticket comments.\n\n## The detection gap is the priority half\n\n`REJECT_STREAK_ALERT` (threshold 3) fired every hour and failed to deliver every time: the\nIAM principal is in account 820258254566, the SNS topic in 896586841071, and no\nresource-based policy permits the cross-account publish. The streak therefore reached 120+\nagainst a threshold of 3 with zero operator signal. Whatever causes the next stall, it is\nequally silent unless a detector exists that does not depend on a remote sink.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 — An on-demand `launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.navapbc.rebar-dev-update`\n  publishes a `current` whose sha equals `origin/main` at that moment. Checked by\n  `readlink ~/.local/state/rebar-dev/current` matching `git ls-remote origin main`, by\n  `grep -c 'Required uv version' ~/.local/state/rebar-dev/update.log` gaining no new line,\n  and by `cat ~/.local/state/rebar-dev/reject-streak` returning 0.\n- [ ] AC2 — The updater selects a uv satisfying the CANDIDATE COMMIT's own\n  `required-version`, read at sync time, rather than any hardcoded absolute path. When no\n  available uv satisfies it, the run fails with a message naming the required version, each\n  version found, and each path inspected. Checked by pointing the resolver at a checkout\n  whose pin no local uv satisfies and observing that message.\n- [ ] AC3 — WITHDRAWN by operator decision: the cross-account SNS authorization is not\n  being pursued and the sink stays as-is. AC4 absorbs the detection requirement.\n- [ ] AC4 — A stalled updater or an over-stale build is detectable locally, with no\n  dependency on the alert path. Checked by `rebar doctor` emitting both a `reject-streak`\n  and a `build-stale` finding on this host, and by\n  `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_doctor_build_freshness.py -q` passing.\n- [ ] AC5 — The pruner's `Directory not empty` failures are resolved and the partial\n  release stub `5fb693345b0cd...1559` is reclaimed. Checked by\n  `ls ~/.local/state/rebar-dev/releases` no longer listing it, and by\n  `~/.local/state/rebar-dev/launchd.err.log` gaining no new `rm:` line after a run.\n\n## Testing\n\nRepository-side (AC4), from a worktree with `.venv/bin` first on `PATH`:\n\n```\npython -m pytest tests/unit/test_doctor_build_freshness.py -q\npython -m pytest tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py -q\nmake lint\nmake typecheck\nrebar doctor\n```\n\nHost-side (AC1, AC2, AC5) cannot be covered by a repository test: `rebar-dev-update.sh` is\nmachine-local and git-ignored, so it lies outside any test's reach. Those are proven by the\nobservations named in their acceptance criteria, run against the live updater, and the\nAC2 resolver is exercised against a harness carrying the real pin.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Do not pin a local update tool. The required uv version moves as `main` moves, so it must\n  be read per candidate commit rather than baked into this host.\n- The pin cannot be widened: `check_uv_pin.py` fails the build when `required-version` is\n  loosened to a range or overridden per call site, because an exact pin is the property\n  under test."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788494512294997001,"uuid":"fab2f1ca-7574-49be-81b7-064f602681fe"}